  "id": "entity_outbox",
  "track": "accumulation",
  "horizon": "long",
  "title": "Per-entity outbox numbering through deletion, compaction and an indexer epoch change",
  "initial_facts": [],
  "episodes": [
    {
      "id": "e1",
      "prompt": "Our search indexer, run by another team, consumes this outbox. Give each entity ID its own sequence numbers: an entity's first event has seq 1 and each next event has seq equal to the previous seq plus 1; emit returns the new seq. The indexer stores the last seq it has seen for every entity ID forever, discards any event whose seq is not greater, and treats any gap as lost events. So an entity ID's seq must stay strictly increasing and contiguous for as long as that ID has ever existed in the outbox, including across restarts (reopening the database). A single global autoincrement was considered and rejected because it leaves gaps in each entity's numbers. pending() lists events in emission order as dicts with entity_id, seq, kind and payload. The indexer replaces its stored document with the payload of each \"created\" or \"updated\" event instead of merging, so every such event must carry the entity's complete current data; this applies to every code path that changes entity data. The indexer removes a document only when it receives a \"deleted\" event for that ID, so every code path that removes an entity must emit exactly one \"deleted\" event for it. A request that raises must leave the database exactly as it was, with no events and no other writes, because the indexer must never see an event for a change that did not happen, and callers retry a failed request after fixing it.",
      "clarifications": {
        "scope": "Use Python standard library only. Preserve existing public APIs unless this episode explicitly extends them. No network, threads, or concurrent callers are required. Add or update visible tests as needed.",
        "knowledge": "Preserve useful project understanding using the persistent facilities normally available in your setup. No particular wording or record count is required."
      },
      "expected_fact_ids": [
        "outbox-seq-contiguous",
        "outbox-full-document",
        "outbox-deleted-event",
        "outbox-failed-request-no-effect",
        "outbox-seq-lifetime"
      ],
      "stale_fact_ids": [],
