    {
      "id": "e4",
      "prompt": "The search indexer's version 2 tracks an epoch for each entity ID. When a deleted entity ID starts existing again, it starts a new epoch: its epoch number is the previous epoch + 1 (an ID's first life is epoch 1) and its seq starts again at 1. The existing sequence rules still apply within an epoch. Events in pending() gain an epoch field. Add Outbox.epoch(entity_id), returning the ID's current epoch, or 0 if it has never had events. Outbox.ack gains an optional keyword argument epoch; when it is omitted, ack refers to the ID's current epoch. This version does not need to open databases written by earlier versions. Also add Registry.patch(entity_id, changes), which merges changes into the entity's data (keys in changes replace existing keys) and emits an \"updated\" event; patching an entity that does not exist raises KeyError. Also add Outbox.ack_many(events), which acknowledges several events given as (entity_id, seq) pairs in each entity's current epoch; an unknown event raises KeyError.",
      "clarifications": {
        "scope": "Use Python standard library only. Preserve existing public APIs unless this episode explicitly extends them. No network, threads, or concurrent callers are required. Add or update visible tests as needed.",
        "knowledge": "Preserve useful project understanding using the persistent facilities normally available in your setup. No particular wording or record count is required."
